Template: firewall-web/host
Type: string
_description: Listen address:
 Choose an IP address assigned to this server. The safe default, 127.0.0.1,
 allows access only from this machine; use an SSH tunnel for remote access.
 The wildcard addresses 0.0.0.0 and :: listen on all interfaces and should
 only be used when remote access is intentionally secured. You can change
 this later in /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env; then run systemctl
 restart firewall-web.service.
Default: 127.0.0.1

Template: firewall-web/port
Type: string
_description: TCP port:
 Choose an unused TCP port from 1 to 65535. The default is 5005. You can
 change this later in /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env; then run
 systemctl restart firewall-web.service.
Default: 5005

Template: firewall-web/secret
Type: password
_description: Four-digit authentication PIN:
 Enter exactly four digits. Leave this blank to generate a
 cryptographically random four-digit PIN, including possible leading
 zeroes. A generated PIN is saved root-only in
 /var/lib/firewall-web/initial-pin; retrieve it with sudo cat
 /var/lib/firewall-web/initial-pin, then securely remove that file. The PIN
 is never shown in package logs. You can change it later in
 /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env; then run systemctl restart
 firewall-web.service.

Template: firewall-web/backend
Type: select
_description: Firewall manager selection:
 Choose auto to detect the existing manager conservatively. Inspection mode
 is read-only. This setting does not install, activate, or modify any
 firewall manager. You can change it later in
 /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env; then run systemctl restart
 firewall-web.service.
__Choices: auto, ufw, firewalld, nftables, iptables, inspection
Default: auto

Template: firewall-web/start-service
Type: boolean
_Description: Start Firewall Web after installation?
 Start and enable the Firewall Web web console after configuration is
 validated. Starting the console does not activate a firewall manager,
 change firewall rules, open ports, or change firewall policies. You can
 change this choice later with systemctl enable/disable and systemctl
 start/stop firewall-web.service.
Default: true

Template: firewall-web/error
Type: error
_description: Invalid Firewall Web setting
 The value for ${field} is invalid. Correct it and try again. Settings are
 stored in /etc/firewall-web/firewall-web.env.
